Name: QuickLaunch
Description: Independent quick-launch rail and notification capsule for iOS 15.0-17.3.1 rootless.
 Adds Drawer Window to System Tools with its original sidebar icon, including circular menu and center actions.
 Hides the Home Screen launcher icon while retaining quicklaunch URL commands and Settings configuration.
 Adds independent ScreenCore drawer URL presets in all menus, with guarded same-process dispatch.
 Adds provider-independent unfinished radial swipe recall, with separate per-mode in-memory App history.
 Adds optional Myrtle 1.5.0 native windows and 37 system/window/plugin actions for every menu.
 Adds radial-only gather/disperse, spiral, wave and fan animations with orbit and original unfold.
 Shows saved choice labels and native checked option lists throughout menu settings.
 Shares bounded prepared icon caches and deduplicated main-thread icon lookups across all menus.
 Preserves excess radial favorites without deleting saved configuration.
 Capsule recent mode keeps the full system App switcher list, including tombstones, and sorts by successful QuickLaunch launch counts.
 Adds five optional Iya split opening modes using its supplied SpringBoard integration API.
 Adds center image connected-background removal with tolerance, smoothing, feathering, undo and non-destructive edit persistence.
 Adds native installed Shortcuts selection and background execution by unique identifier, without opening the Shortcuts app.
 Adds guarded optional SVP 1.4.2 opening and seventeen native toolbar actions in all menus.
 Adds automatic brightness, Night Shift, True Tone and independent region screenshot selection.
 Follow the foreground App interface orientation and independently choose recent background Apps or saved favorites per menu.
 Capsule notification icons retain native notification actions and use a 1-120 second duration slider.
 New notifications reveal the capsule in recent and favorite modes; ordinary and radial menus are unchanged.
 Recent rail and capsule shrink to live App count, retaining viewport limits and overflow scrolling.
 Synchronizes cross-process menu preferences and shows a dedicated recent/favorite selection page.
 Compensates the actual overlay host transform to prevent duplicate landscape rotation.
 Preserves favorite Apps and actions when switching content sources.
 Adds 21 shared tools including acknowledged screen recording, accessibility actions and optional Open window management.
 Shared tool dispatch validates runtime method encodings and uses the same lock-state sources as overlay visibility.
 Separate system tools, URLs and Shortcuts lists for each rail, capsule and radial menu.
 Radial apps, tools, URLs and Shortcuts share consecutive slots across the same concentric rings.
 Consecutive circular app and action slots with adjustable spacing; rail and capsule actions appear inline beside apps.
 Shared custom URL images or name tiles in every menu.
 Host-aware SpringBoard and LaunchServices URL dispatch with ordinary app fallback and failure feedback.
 Customizable center icon with an independent app, tool, URL or Shortcut binding and photo/file artwork.
 Edit center photo/file artwork with circular preview, drag positioning, pinch or slider zoom, reset, cancel and save.
 Transparent center artwork with independent size, slow rotation, silhouette glow and outward light waves.
 Shared square or circular icon frames across all quick menus and radial previews.
 Choose fullscreen, PullOver-X, ScreenCore, Open, FV or SVP split windows independently for all menus.
 Optional TrollOpenJB 1.5.2 bridge with runtime ABI checks, preserving its window limits.
 Optional floatingView 1.6.0-6 bridge using its in-process app-opening notification.
 Optional independent radial menu with progressive swipe reveal, bounce and haptic feedback.
 Circular menu supports 68 combined apps and actions, concentric rings, stronger adjustable bounce and persistent invisible touch regions.
 Choose left or right radial activation with mirrored swipe animation and debug touch regions.
 Group related preferences into module pages, with optional timed hold to open radial apps fullscreen.
 Automatically remove confirmed unavailable apps from all menus, preserving URLs and valid app records.
 Adapt radial menus and debug touch regions to landscape, with independent landscape dimensions and position.
 Optionally show the capsule only in landscape; scroll unlimited capsule apps within four landscape slots and one to ten portrait slots.
 Expose a guarded optional SpringBoard bridge for the floating ball to present one selected menu.
 Long-press a visible floating ball in apps or on Home to explicitly present a menu, with temporary keyboard and capsule portrait overrides.
 Adjust docked capsule artwork opacity from 0 to 100 percent while preserving invisible touch targets.
 Optionally retain one to three empty Home Screen pages after existing pages.
 Keep two overlays with separate apps and settings, adapting to portrait and landscape.
 Select any number of rail apps; scroll within a fixed eight-slot viewport.
 Tap notification apps to open and remove them; long-press for the full list.
 Both overlays share the lock-screen switch and hide for the keyboard unless explicitly presented by a ball long press.
 The border turns green when charging and red below 20 percent battery.
 Dock shapes restore their original safe-area spacing, with touch targets around the artwork.
 Five adaptive dock shapes include a short bar, thermometer, dot and pill.
 Includes battery/temperature border modes, adjustable icons and a Chinese user guide.
